# Guidelines for Rule Creation

Read and follow this file whenever the user asks to create, edit, rename, or reorganize Cursor rules.

## Naming Convention

- Format: `NNN-kebab-case-topic.mdc` (e.g. `002-frontend-components.mdc`)
- Use the next available three-digit prefix; never reuse numbers
- `000` is reserved for this file

## What Belongs Where

| Content | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Shared project truth | `AGENTS.md` or domain `frontend/AGENTS.md` / `backend/AGENTS.md` |
| Tool-specific scoping only | `.mdc` body after the `@import` |
| Personal preferences | Cursor user rules or `CLAUDE.local.md` |
| Repeatable workflows | Skills, not rules |

## Required Frontmatter

```yaml
---
description: Brief description of what this rule does
alwaysApply: true   # OR globs: <pattern>
---
```

- Include `description`
- Use `alwaysApply: true` for universal rules, or `globs: <pattern>` for file-scoped rules
- Do not set both unless a scoped rule explicitly needs `alwaysApply: false`

## Import Pattern

Prefer importing canonical docs instead of duplicating content:

- Root: `@../../AGENTS.md`
- Domain: `@../../frontend/AGENTS.md` or `@../../backend/AGENTS.md`

Put only Cursor-specific notes in the rule body after the import.

## Before Creating

1. Confirm purpose and scope (always apply vs file-specific)
2. If file-specific, confirm glob patterns (e.g. `frontend/**/*.tsx`)
3. One concern per rule; target under 50 lines of body content

## After Creating

1. Add a one-line entry to the **Cursor Rules** section in `AGENTS.md` (number, name, scope)
2. Update domain `AGENTS.md` if the rule reflects an architectural decision

## Checklist

- [ ] File is `.mdc` in `.cursor/rules/`
- [ ] Correct three-digit prefix assigned
- [ ] Frontmatter valid (`description` + scope)
- [ ] No duplicated AGENTS content
- [ ] `AGENTS.md` Cursor Rules section updated
